>## Angle bracket pair `<` `>` for use with `brackets`
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term angleBraces = ast.Brackets{open = ast.Symbol{"<"}, close = ast.Symbol{">"}}
#^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
#    ^ source.hydra
#     ^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.function.hydra
#                ^ source.hydra
#                 ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.equals.hydra
#                  ^ source.hydra
#                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.type.nominal.hydra
#                               ^ source.hydra
#                                ^^^^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                                    ^ source.hydra
#                                     ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.equals.hydra
#                                      ^ source.hydra
#                                       ^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.type.nominal.hydra
#                                                 ^ source.hydra
#                                                  ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra punctuation.definition.string.begin.hydra
#                                                   ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra
#                                                    ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra punctuation.definition.string.end.hydra
#                                                     ^^^ source.hydra
#                                                        ^^^^^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                                                             ^ source.hydra
#                                                              ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.equals.hydra
#                                                               ^ source.hydra
#                                                                ^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.type.nominal.hydra
#                                                                          ^ source.hydra
#                                                                           ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra punctuation.definition.string.begin.hydra
#                                                                            ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra
#                                                                             ^ source.hydra string.quoted.double.hydra punctuation.definition.string.end.hydra
#                                                                              ^^^ source.hydra
>
>## Comma-separate the elements inside angle brackets in the given block style; renders as `<>` when empty
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term angleBracesList = λstyle,els.logic.ifElse (lists.isEmpty els) (cst "<>") (brackets angleBraces style (commaSep style els))
#^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
#    ^ source.hydra
#     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.function.hydra
#                    ^ source.hydra
#                     ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.equals.hydra
#                      ^ source.hydra
#                       ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.lambda.hydra
